  67:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *
  68:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** * \brief Sets the drive mode for each of the Pins component's pins.
  69:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** * 
  70:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** * <b>Note</b> This affects all pins in the Pins component instance. Use the
  71:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** * Per-Pin APIs if you wish to control individual pin's drive modes.
  72:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *
  73:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** * \param mode
  74:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *  Mode for the selected signals. Valid options are documented in 
  75:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *  \ref driveMode.
  76:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *
  77:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** * \return
  78:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *  None
  79:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *
  80:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** * \sideeffect
  81:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *  If you use read-modify-write operations that are not atomic, the ISR can
  82:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *  cause corruption of this function. An ISR that interrupts this function 
  83:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *  and performs writes to the Pins component Drive Mode registers can cause 
  84:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *  corrupted port data. To avoid this issue, you should either use the Per-Pin
  85:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *  APIs (primary method) or disable interrupts around this function.
  86:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** *
  87:Generated_Source\PSoC5/Vref.c **** * \funcusage
